<node id="Glucose Hypometabolism and Synaptic Dysfunction">
  <data key="d0">mechanism</data>
  <data key="d1">Reduced neuronal and synaptic activity in the AD brain is observed as hypometabolism, particularly in temporoparietal and posterior cingulate cortices. This metabolic impairment is captured by FDG-PET imaging showing reduced glucose uptake and is closely associated with ongoing cognitive and functional decline in AD patients.</data>
  <data key="d2">34</data>
</node>
