<node id="Cognitive Decline and Executive Dysfunction">
  <data key="d0">mechanism</data>
  <data key="d1">Clinical progression of AD is manifested by a continuum of global cognitive impairment, episodic memory loss, language difficulties, visuospatial deficits, and executive dysfunction. Clinical and neuropsychological tests (e.g., MMSE, MoCA, AVLT, Digit Span, category fluency, Trail Making, ADAS-Cog) assess the severity and domain-specific aspects of cognitive decline reflected in baseline diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d2">65</data>
</node>
