</node>
<node id="Demographic and Genetic Susceptibility">
  <data key="d0">mechanism</data>
  <data key="d1">Age remains the strongest risk factor for AD. Other socio-demographic variables (education, gender, ethnicity, marital status, race) modulate risk and disease manifestation, both through genetic predisposition and environmental/lifestyle factors. Lower education may decrease cognitive reserve, increasing vulnerability to symptomatic AD. Diverse demographic data help identify at-risk groups, inform stratification, and address population differences in AD susceptibility.</data>
  <data key="d2">28</data>
</node>
